findings:
- finding_id: I1
  title: Dependencies inline instead of workspace level
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Dev added chrono and uuid as inline dependencies in Cargo.toml. Reviewer
    flagged unused dependencies but not the inline-vs-workspace issue.
- finding_id: I2
  title: 'FieldErrorCode missing #[non_exhaustive]'
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer finding #7: '#[non_exhaustive] missing on public types \u2014\
    \ response.rs:14,21,29' flags missing #[non_exhaustive] on public types including\
    \ enums/structs. However, this specifically calls out ApiEnvelope/EnvelopeError/EnvelopeMeta,\
    \ not FieldErrorCode. Partial catch at best, but the principle was flagged."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Hardcoded trace_id 'none'
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: 'Reviewer finding #11 verified that meta.trace_id is ''present'' but did
    not flag that it''s hardcoded to ''none'' rather than derived from request context.
    The rate_limit trace_id issue (finding #9) is tangential but doesn''t address
    the ResponseMeta hardcoding.'
- finding_id: I4
  title: Zero structured logging
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer finding #4: 'No structured logging or tracing anywhere \u2014\
    \ all src/*.rs. Zero tracing::info!(), tracing::error!(), tracing::warn!(), or\
    \ #[tracing::instrument] calls exist.'"
- finding_id: I5
  title: Security comment claims tracing that doesn't exist
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: 'Reviewer flagged zero logging (finding #4) but did not specifically call
    out misleading SECURITY comments claiming logging exists when it doesn''t.'
- finding_id: I6
  title: Non-ASCII tenant header silently treated as missing
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No test was written for non-ASCII tenant header values. TEA's auth tests
    cover valid/missing/expired/malformed tokens but not non-ASCII header edge cases.
- finding_id: I7
  title: "CWE-209 test gap \u2014 no body assertion"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: "TEA wrote CWE-209 tests in api_security.rs and they passed, but the pipeline\
    \ output doesn't indicate body content assertions were included \u2014 only status\
    \ code checking is mentioned."
- finding_id: I8
  title: CORS preflight test doesn't verify CORS headers
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No CORS preflight test appears in any test file. CORS is not mentioned
    in TEA's test plan or reviewer findings as a tested area.
- finding_id: I9
  title: "Wrong log levels \u2014 error! for 4xx client errors"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Since I4 (zero logging) was flagged but not fixed, the wrong-log-levels
    issue never arose. No phase addressed appropriate log level selection for 4xx
    vs 5xx.
- finding_id: I10
  title: CORS allows Any origin/method/header (CWE-942)
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No CORS configuration was reviewed or tested. Neither TEA, Dev, nor Reviewer
    mentioned CORS origin/method/header restrictions or CWE-942.
